// A GNU statement-expression body carries one exact outer semantic scope.
// Before its typed expression owner exists this is a bounded construction
// transaction; after adoption it is a persistent semantic edge independent
// of the expression's structural ancestry.  Ordinary blocks continue to
// derive their scope exclusively from structural ownership.
